if {Object} == "Medication":
	H\: Hm. Medication is always the answer, right doc...? Pfft. A bandaid, if you ask me. You want to fix me? You fix the cause.
elif {Object} == "Blood":
	H\: What the—? Did I do this? Keep having nosebleeds when I’m half asleep. Can barely fucking remember having them.
elif {Object} == "LetterOfApology":
	H\: Hm. Never got around to sending this. Hope she knows I’m sorry for what I did. Just want to make things right... I’ll find them, Angelie. I promise.
elif {Object} == "Phone":
	I’m ready to make a call.
elif {Object} == "Door":
	I can't leave yet
elif {Object} == "ComputerDesk":
	if Progress.can_desk == true:
		Everyone I suspect should be clearly labelled. Each file should have a piece of potential evidence I sourced from... Guh. I can’t remember... the station? No... that can’t be right...
		label Files
		- August
			label AugustFiles
			- August's File
				August Williams. Angelie’s girlfriend. I remember reading 99% of murders are committed by the victim’s girlfriend online somewhere... I think that’s the right stat.
				do Signals.emit("reading_started", "AUG_1")
			- August-Angelie Transcript | [=""]
				Oh yeah. This is the transcript of August’s last call with Angelie. Three days before the murder... Can’t remember how I got this either...
				do Signals.emit("reading_started", "AUG_ANG_TRANSCRIPT")
			Hm. A few things stand out. The computer’s still hooked up to the RCPD’s surveillance and information database. I should search for something, or maybe look at another file.
			August Williams. Let me look at her file and that transcript again.
		- Vincent
			label VincentFiles
			- Vincent's File
				Vincent O’Brien. Angelie and I’s ol’ supervisor. A real cunt. I remember the tone he spoke to me when he dismissed me. Like I was some child... What goes around, eh?
				do Signals.emit("reading_started", "VIN_1")
			- Dismissal - Vincent
				I got the case summary of his termination here as well... Look at that. Exactly 12 years after I was dismissed. No such thing as a coincidence.
				do Signals.emit("reading_started", "VIN_DISMISSAL")
			Pretty short. Might find more if I input the file number into the computer. It’s still hooked up to the RCPD’s surveillance and information database. Or, I could look at another file.
			Vince O’Brien. I can read his file and case summary again.
		- Orlando
			label OrlandoFiles
			- Orlando's File
				Orlando Martin. Ex-con. One of the guys Angelie and I put away. Couldn’t believe how weak his sentence was after he was found guilty... what did he do again?
				do Signals.emit("reading_started", "ORL_1")
			- Orlando's Record
				Oh yeah. I remember finding that weird, her visiting him at RC Penitentiary. Said she could ‘save him’. I know they started recording all visitations. There might be something on his behavioural record.
				do Signals.emit("reading_started", "ORL_RECORD")
			I should look up those file names on my computer. It’s still hooked up to the RCPD’s surveillance and information database. Maybe I’ll find something in the transcripts. I could also check out the other files.
			Orlando Martin. I could take a look at his file and record again.
		[wait time="0.2"]
		- Read another File
			jump Files
		- Maybe Later
	else:
		My head’s still pounding. I need a coffee before I get to work.
elif {Object} == "Files":
	if Progress.can_file == true:
		Okay. Let’s check these out.
		Everyone I suspect should be clearly labelled. Each file should have a piece of potential evidence I sourced from... Guh. I can’t remember... the station? No... that can’t be right...
elif {Object} == "Phone":
	if Progress.can_phone == false:
		I’m not ready to make any calls yet. I should check out each suspect’s file.
elif {Object} == "Computer":
	if Progress.can_computer == false:
		I’m not ready to do any research yet. I should check out each suspect’s file.
elif {Object} == "LukewarmCoffee":
	That’s it. That’s the stuff. Feels like the only time I feel normal’s after a cup of coffee... Let’s get to work.
elif {Object} == "Phone":
	if Progress.can_phone == true:
		I’m ready to make a call.
		- Call Orlando
		- Call Vincent
		- Call August
	else:
		I’m not ready to make a call yet.